WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.647
Enrollment automation, starting
with the third correction

2
00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:06.525
to the Federal Modernization
Workbook's Book 07.

3
00:00:06.525 --> 00:00:12.701
Book 07 Chapter 08 says CyberArk documents
that the win-acme client needs FIPS mode

4
00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:18.787
off, and advises using another tested client
where the server must run in FIPS mode.

5
00:00:18.787 --> 00:00:22.863
The 26.1 Installation and
Upgrade Guide is broader.

6
00:00:22.863 --> 00:00:27.049
It says that because FIPS is
not supported for ACMEv2,

7
00:00:27.049 --> 00:00:31.425
you can't have FIPS enabled on
any server used for ACMEv2.

8
00:00:31.425 --> 00:00:34.129
The topic page still names only win-acme;

9
00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:38.063
the stricter text governs
until CyberArk says otherwise.

10
00:00:38.063 --> 00:00:43.761
The program's design guidance: run the ACME
service on dedicated servers that aren't

11
00:00:43.761 --> 00:00:48.800
in FIPS mode, kept out of the FIPS-mode
set, or get a written vendor statement.

12
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.650
Book 07 has been updated to match.

13
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:59.676
The ACME service itself implements RFC
8555 with http-01 and dns-01 challenges,

14
00:00:59.676 --> 00:01:05.850
and was designed and tested with
certbot, win-acme and acme.sh.

15
00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:10.587
The page both lists wildcard issuance
and calls it future work, so test it.

16
00:01:10.587 --> 00:01:16.823
EST runs on port 50443 with client-certificate
authentication, and a CA label in

17
00:01:16.823 --> 00:01:22.963
the URL selects the CA template; three
optional EST functions aren't supported.

18
00:01:22.963 --> 00:01:26.488
SCEP, for network devices, needs port 80.

19
00:01:26.488 --> 00:01:30.947
For everything else there's
the REST API with OAuth tokens,

20
00:01:30.947 --> 00:01:35.778
and CyberArk's vCert command-line
tool, currently version 5.13.9,

21
00:01:35.778 --> 00:01:39.587
which needs view, read,
write and create on its zone.

22
00:01:39.587 --> 00:01:43.435
Agentless drivers push
certificates to the endpoints,

23
00:01:43.435 --> 00:01:47.951
licensed per instance in 26.1, and
the Server Agent covers the rest.

24
00:01:47.951 --> 00:01:53.056
Sources: CyberArk 26.1
Installation and Upgrade Guide p.

25
00:01:53.056 --> 00:02:00.048
50; ACME overview; EST overview,
limitations and reference; Configuring SCEP;

26
00:02:00.048 --> 00:02:05.375
NDE rules; Setting up OAuth;
System Requirements; What's New;

27
00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:10.100
vCert README and latest
release; Book 07, Chapter 08.
